{"title":"Career Roadmap · Restoration Specialist","role":"Restoration Specialist","summary":"A Restoration Specialist works on the assessment, conservation and restoration of historic buildings, monuments and culturally significant structures. The role combines architecture, architectural history, building pathology, traditional construction techniques, materials science, documentation and conservation practice.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Arch (Bachelor of Architecture)","Course":"Heritage Conservation Architecture"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Restoration Specialist works on the assessment, conservation and restoration of historic buildings, monuments and culturally significant structures. The role combines architecture, architectural history, building pathology, traditional construction techniques, materials science, documentation and conservation practice."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Arch graduate, this is a specialized career path. A strong foundation in heritage conservation is important, but advanced restoration projects often benefit from a specialized M.Arch/PG in Conservation, Heritage Management, Building Conservation or a related field, combined with field experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Surveying historic buildings"},{"text":"Documenting existing conditions"},{"text":"Identifying deterioration and defects"},{"text":"Studying historical construction"},{"text":"Assessing traditional materials"},{"text":"Preparing conservation drawings"},{"text":"Developing restoration strategies"},{"text":"Coordinating conservation works"},{"text":"Specifying compatible repair materials"},{"text":"Monitoring restoration work"},{"text":"Recording interventions"},{"text":"Supporting adaptive-reuse projects"},{"text":"Coordinating with archaeologists, engineers, historians and craftspeople"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Typical career progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Arch","Heritage Conservation Knowledge","Conservation / Restoration Intern","Junior Conservation Architect / Restoration Assistant","Restoration Specialist","Senior Conservation Specialist","Conservation Project Lead","Heritage Conservation Consultant","Conservation Practice / Research Leadership"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Architecture + history fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Building materials + documentation"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Heritage conservation + building pathology"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Restoration projects + field internship"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Conservation Assistant / Junior Restoration Professional"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Restoration Specialist / Conservation Architect"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Conservation Specialist"}],[{"text":"8+ years"},{"text":"Conservation Consultant / Project Lead"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-Wise Roadmap","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Architecture + Architectural History"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong foundation in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Architectural design"},{"text":"History of architecture"},{"text":"Building construction"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Structures"},{"text":"Measured drawing"},{"text":"Architectural documentation"},{"text":"Visual representation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Start studying"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Historic architectural styles"},{"text":"Regional architecture"},{"text":"Traditional building systems"},{"text":"Vernacular architecture"},{"text":"Historic urban settlements"},{"text":"Cultural significance"},{"text":"Develop the habit of observing buildings as physical evidence of history, rather than studying architectural history only through textbooks."}]}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Building Materials & Documentation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The student should develop strong skills in documenting existing buildings."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Measured surveys"},{"text":"Architectural photography"},{"text":"Hand documentation"},{"text":"AutoCAD documentation"},{"text":"Building materials"},{"text":"Traditional masonry"},{"text":"Timber construction"},{"text":"Lime-based construction"},{"text":"Stone construction"},{"text":"Traditional roofing"},{"text":"Basic structural behaviour"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Documentation workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Historic Building","Site Visit","Measurement","Photography","Material Identification","Condition Mapping","Measured Drawings","Historic Documentation"]}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Conservation & Building Pathology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is the major specialization stage."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn conservation principles"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Significance"},{"text":"Authenticity"},{"text":"Integrity"},{"text":"Minimal intervention"},{"text":"Reversibility where appropriate"},{"text":"Compatibility"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Distinguishing old and new interventions"},{"text":"Adaptive reuse"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact treatment depends on the significance, materials and condition of each building; restoration should not become an automatic replacement exercise."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn building pathology"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cracks"},{"text":"Dampness"},{"text":"Rising damp"},{"text":"Water penetration"},{"text":"Salt deposits"},{"text":"Biological growth"},{"text":"Timber deterioration"},{"text":"Stone deterioration"},{"text":"Mortar failure"},{"text":"Plaster failure"},{"text":"Roof damage"},{"text":"Structural movement"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Diagnostic workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Observed Defect","Site Investigation","Material Identification","Possible Cause","Further Testing","Diagnosis","Conservation Strategy","Repair / Restoration","Monitoring"]},{"type":"p","text":"The critical professional skill is diagnosis before intervention."}]},{"heading":"Year 4 — Restoration Practice","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Work on complete conservation/restoration studies."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Conservation documentation"},{"text":"Condition assessment"},{"text":"Material mapping"},{"text":"Damage mapping"},{"text":"Restoration drawings"},{"text":"Specifications"},{"text":"Conservation reports"},{"text":"Cost estimation"},{"text":"Tender documentation"},{"text":"Site supervision"},{"text":"Craft coordination"},{"text":"Heritage interpretation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Historical Research","Architectural Survey","Condition Assessment","Material Investigation","Significance Assessment","Conservation Strategy","Restoration Design","Specifications + BOQ","Site Implementation","Monitoring + Documentation"]}]},{"heading":"Core Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Target Level"],"rows":[[{"text":"Architectural Design"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Architectural History"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Heritage Conservation"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Measured Survey"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Building Documentation"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Building Pathology"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Traditional Materials"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Conservation Theory"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Restoration Documentation"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Architectural Photography"},{"text":"Intermediate–Advanced"}],[{"text":"CAD"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"BIM"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Intermediate–Advanced"}],[{"text":"Photogrammetry"},{"text":"Intermediate–Advanced"}],[{"text":"3D Scanning"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Structural Fundamentals"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Materials Testing"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Technical Reporting"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Site Supervision"},{"text":"Advanced"}]]}]},{"heading":"Software & Digital Tools","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Documentation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"Revit"},{"text":"SketchUp"},{"text":"Rhino"}]},{"type":"h","text":"GIS"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"ArcGIS or equivalent GIS workflows"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use GIS for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Heritage mapping"},{"text":"Site analysis"},{"text":"Urban context"},{"text":"Historic districts"},{"text":"Cultural landscape documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Photogrammetry"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn workflows using tools such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"RealityCapture"},{"text":"Agisoft Metashape"},{"text":"Meshroom"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3D documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"LiDAR"},{"text":"3D laser scanning"},{"text":"Photogrammetry"},{"text":"Point clouds"},{"text":"Orthophotos"},{"text":"3D mesh generation"},{"text":"The important skill is understanding the survey-to-documentation workflow, not simply knowing one software package."}]}]},{"heading":"Major Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Historic Building Documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"Select an existing historic structure and prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Site survey"},{"text":"Photographic documentation"},{"text":"Measured drawings"},{"text":"Floor plans"},{"text":"Elevations"},{"text":"Sections"},{"text":"Architectural details"},{"text":"Material inventory"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Condition Assessment"},{"type":"p","text":"Map defects on a historic building."},{"type":"p","text":"Document:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cracks"},{"text":"Dampness"},{"text":"Biological growth"},{"text":"Material loss"},{"text":"Plaster deterioration"},{"text":"Roof problems"},{"text":"Create a condition map."}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Building Elevation","Defect Identification","Defect Classification","Condition Mapping","Severity Assessment"]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Material Conservation Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Study a traditional building material such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lime mortar"},{"text":"Stone"},{"text":"Brick"},{"text":"Timber"},{"text":"Traditional plaster"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Original composition"},{"text":"Construction method"},{"text":"Deterioration"},{"text":"Compatible repair options"},{"text":"Maintenance requirements"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Restoration Proposal"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare a complete restoration strategy for a historic building."},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Historical research"},{"text":"Significance assessment"},{"text":"Existing drawings"},{"text":"Condition assessment"},{"text":"Intervention philosophy"},{"text":"Proposed restoration"},{"text":"Material specifications"},{"text":"BOQ"},{"text":"Implementation phases"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Adaptive Reuse"},{"type":"p","text":"Take a historic building and propose a new use while retaining its heritage value."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Historic residence → cultural centre"},{"text":"Warehouse → creative workspace"},{"text":"Heritage building → museum"},{"text":"Historic institutional building → public facility"},{"text":"The project should demonstrate that reuse does not require unnecessary loss of historic fabric."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 6 — Digital Heritage Documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"Combine:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Drone photography where legally and safely applicable"},{"text":"Photogrammetry"},{"text":"3D scanning"},{"text":"Point clouds"},{"text":"BIM"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Create a digital record of the heritage structure."}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Roadmap","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1–2"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Architecture firms"},{"text":"Heritage documentation projects"},{"text":"Museums"},{"text":"Cultural institutions"},{"text":"Architectural history research projects"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Architectural history"},{"text":"Measured drawings"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2–3"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Conservation architecture firms"},{"text":"Heritage consultants"},{"text":"Restoration contractors"},{"text":"Archaeological/cultural heritage organizations"},{"text":"Research institutions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Condition assessment"},{"text":"Material identification"},{"text":"Survey methods"},{"text":"Conservation documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3–4"},{"type":"p","text":"Target specialized positions:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Conservation Architecture Intern"},{"text":"Heritage Documentation Intern"},{"text":"Restoration Intern"},{"text":"Heritage Research Intern"},{"text":"Building Conservation Intern"},{"text":"Conservation Site Intern"},{"text":"Field exposure is extremely important. Restoration is not a purely studio-based profession."}]}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Job Titles","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The exact title \"Restoration Specialist\" may not be used at entry level."},{"type":"p","text":"Search for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Conservation Architect"},{"text":"Junior Conservation Architect"},{"text":"Restoration Architect"},{"text":"Conservation Assistant"},{"text":"Heritage Documentation Specialist"},{"text":"Heritage Consultant"},{"text":"Restoration Assistant"},{"text":"Conservation Project Assistant"},{"text":"Historic Building Surveyor"},{"text":"Heritage Research Assistant"},{"text":"Building Conservation Specialist"},{"text":"Heritage Site Coordinator"}]}]},{"heading":"Employer Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Employer Type","Important Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Conservation Architecture Firm"},{"text":"Survey + conservation design"}],[{"text":"Restoration Consultancy"},{"text":"Building pathology + materials"}],[{"text":"Heritage Organization"},{"text":"Documentation + research"}],[{"text":"Museum / Cultural Institution"},{"text":"Heritage documentation"}],[{"text":"Government Heritage Projects"},{"text":"Survey + conservation documentation"}],[{"text":"Restoration Contractor"},{"text":"Materials + site execution"}],[{"text":"Archaeological Organization"},{"text":"Documentation + conservation"}],[{"text":"University / Research Lab"},{"text":"Research + digital documentation"}],[{"text":"Urban Heritage Consultancy"},{"text":"GIS + historic urban analysis"}],[{"text":"Adaptive Reuse Practice"},{"text":"Conservation + contemporary design"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Training","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful training areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Heritage conservation"},{"text":"Historic building documentation"},{"text":"Building pathology"},{"text":"Traditional construction"},{"text":"Lime technology"},{"text":"Stone conservation"},{"text":"Timber conservation"},{"text":"Photogrammetry"},{"text":"3D laser scanning"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Heritage management"},{"text":"Conservation project management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Particularly valuable practical training"},{"type":"p","text":"A student should try to obtain hands-on experience with traditional materials and crafts, such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Lime mortar"},{"text":"Lime plaster"},{"text":"Masonry repair"},{"text":"Stonework"},{"text":"Timber repair"},{"text":"Traditional roofing"},{"text":"Digital skills are valuable, but they should complement physical understanding of historic buildings."}]}]},{"heading":"Higher Education Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For this career, postgraduate specialization is strongly recommended if the student wants to become a specialist rather than remain a general architect working occasionally on heritage projects."},{"type":"table","header":["PG Area","Relevance"],"rows":[[{"text":"M.Arch Conservation"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"M.Arch Heritage Conservation"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Building Conservation"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Heritage Management"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Historic Preservation"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Architectural Conservation"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Heritage Studies"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Architectural History"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Archaeology / Heritage Studies"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Building Pathology"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Arch","Heritage / Conservation Projects","Conservation Internship","M.Arch / PG in Conservation","Junior Conservation Professional","Restoration Specialist","Senior Conservation Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"For highly specialized research, documentation or conservation-science positions, further research training may be appropriate."}]},{"heading":"Specialization Paths","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Path A — Historic Building Restoration"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Arch","Building Documentation","Building Pathology","Traditional Materials","Restoration Projects","Restoration Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"Best for students interested in hands-on restoration."},{"type":"h","text":"Path B — Conservation Architecture"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Arch","Heritage Conservation","M.Arch Conservation","Conservation Projects","Conservation Architect","Senior Conservation Consultant"]},{"type":"h","text":"Path C — Digital Heritage"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Arch","Heritage Documentation","Photogrammetry","3D Scanning","HBIM","Digital Heritage Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"This is one of the strongest emerging combinations for architecture graduates."},{"type":"h","text":"Path D — Conservation Science"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Arch","Building Materials","Material Testing","Building Pathology","Conservation Science","Research / Technical Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"This path may require substantial postgraduate/research training."},{"type":"h","text":"Path E — Adaptive Reuse"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Arch","Heritage Conservation","Historic Building Assessment","Adaptive Reuse","Heritage + Contemporary Design","Adaptive Reuse Consultant"]}]},{"heading":"Emerging Technologies","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"1. HBIM — Historic Building Information Modelling"},{"type":"p","text":"HBIM combines heritage documentation with BIM."},{"type":"flow","items":["Historic Building","Survey","Photogrammetry / Laser Scan","Point Cloud","HBIM Model","Condition + Material Data","Conservation Management"]},{"type":"p","text":"This is becoming an important digital skill for heritage professionals."},{"type":"h","text":"2. 3D Laser Scanning"},{"type":"p","text":"Laser scanners can capture complex geometry and produce point clouds for documentation and analysis."},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Irregular structures"},{"text":"Sculptural details"},{"text":"Historic façades"},{"text":"Deformed geometry"},{"text":"Difficult-to-measure spaces"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Photogrammetry"},{"type":"p","text":"Photographs can be processed into:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Orthophotos"},{"text":"3D meshes"},{"text":"Point clouds"},{"text":"Digital elevations"},{"text":"This is particularly useful for detailed heritage documentation."}]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Digital Heritage Archives"},{"type":"p","text":"Future conservation projects increasingly maintain structured digital records containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Building"},{"text":"├── Historical Data"},{"text":"├── Drawings"},{"text":"├── Materials"},{"text":"├── Defects"},{"text":"├── Interventions"},{"text":"├── Photographs"},{"text":"├── 3D Model"},{"text":"└── Maintenance History"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. AI-Assisted Condition Assessment"},{"type":"p","text":"Computer vision can potentially assist with identifying:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cracks"},{"text":"Surface deterioration"},{"text":"Biological growth"},{"text":"Material loss"},{"text":"Moisture-related damage"},{"text":"However, automated detection should support—not replace—professional diagnosis."}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Digital Twins for Heritage"},{"type":"p","text":"A digital heritage model can combine:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"HBIM"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Sensors"},{"text":"Historical documentation"},{"text":"Condition data"},{"text":"Maintenance records"},{"text":"to support long-term conservation management."}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Minimum employability stack"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Arch"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Architectural History"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Heritage Conservation Fundamentals"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Measured Survey"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Building Pathology"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Traditional Materials"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"SketchUp / Revit"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Heritage Documentation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Conservation Portfolio"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Field Internship"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong candidate stack"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Arch"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Heritage Conservation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"M.Arch / PG Conservation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Building Pathology"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Traditional Materials"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Conservation Theory"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Measured Survey"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"AutoCAD + Revit"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Photogrammetry"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"3D Laser Scanning"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"HBIM"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Restoration Documentation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Site Execution"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Professional Field Experience"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should be able to take a historic building through the initial stages of professional conservation assessment."},{"type":"flow","items":["Historic Building","Historical Research","Measured Survey","Photographic Documentation","Material Identification","Condition Mapping","Building Pathology","Significance Assessment","Conservation Strategy","Restoration Proposal","Specifications + BOQ","Site Monitoring"]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio target"},{"type":"p","text":"Build at least 5 strong projects:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Historic building documentation"},{"text":"Condition/damage mapping"},{"text":"Traditional material study"},{"text":"Restoration proposal"},{"text":"Adaptive reuse project"},{"text":"An additional photogrammetry/HBIM project can significantly differentiate the portfolio."}]},{"type":"p","text":"Every major project should demonstrate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Historical research"},{"text":"Existing-condition drawings"},{"text":"Photographs"},{"text":"Material analysis"},{"text":"Defect mapping"},{"text":"Conservation rationale"},{"text":"Proposed intervention"},{"text":"Technical details"},{"text":"Implementation considerations"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest professional positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Architect","Conservation Specialist","Building Pathology","Digital Heritage"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"rather than simply:"},{"type":"h","text":"Architect who works on old buildings"},{"type":"p","text":"The differentiating capability is the ability to understand why a historic building is deteriorating, how its original materials and construction work, what intervention is appropriate, and how to document and manage that intervention."},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Architecture"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Architectural History"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Building Pathology"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Traditional Materials"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Conservation Theory"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Survey & Documentation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Digital Heritage"},{"text":"+"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Site Experience","Restoration Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"This creates a realistic progression toward Restoration Specialist → Senior Conservation Specialist → Conservation Project Lead → Heritage Conservation Consultant, with adjacent opportunities in adaptive reuse, historic building surveying, HBIM, digital heritage, conservation research and restoration project management."}]}]}